Patch 002: env-forced fuse_gemm_comms (async TP) + construction-site diagnostics.

Why: the partner's golden argv carries pass_config {"fuse_gemm_comms": true}
and his private wheel honors it; public v0.27.0 silently drops it on the Ray
path (issue #1 on his repo). fuse_gemm_comms = async TP = allreduce/compute
overlap - the single biggest latency-bound slice of the decode step per the
glm52-spark-kit decode profile (~30 ms/step of collectives). It force-enables
sequence parallelism internally, so memory is watched on first boot.

Mechanics: env var instead of fixing the plumbing blind - workers inherit the
container environment no matter how many times VllmConfig gets rebuilt between
API layer and EngineCore, so this works even before we locate the exact drop
point; the two log branches tell us whether user pass_config survived to each
construction site. Unset => byte-identical stock.

Boot usage: add VLLM_FORCE_FUSE_GEMM_COMMS=1 to the serve container env.
First boot MUST run the correctness gate x4/x8 and watch MemAvailable.

Applies to vllm v0.27.0 (vllm/config/compilation.py).
